Note status only catches IllegalStateException around the ownership call (Status.java:80), so the SecurityException propagates and the command fails outright rather than degrading.

Two caveats worth knowing:

- gcstats mutates state. It calls gcProxy.getAndResetStats() — a no-arg getter, so JMX exposes it as attribute AndResetStats. A readonly user reading it resets the node's GC counters, clobbering them for anyone else polling.
- queryNames dependency. tablestats, tpstats, tablehistograms, compactionstats, datapaths, getcompactionthreshold enumerate MBeans first. Fine under file-based readonly, but under Cassandra's internal JMX authorizer a role granted only SELECT and not DESCRIBE will fail on these.

